n\nWe observe that Joint SAN outperforms the SAN baseline with a large margin, e.g., 67.89 vs 69.27 (+1.38) and 70.68 vs 72.20 (+1.52) in\n\nBy incorporating the output information of classifier into Joint SAN, it obtains a slight improvement, e.g., 72.2 vs 72.66 (+0.46) in terms of F1 score.\n\nComparing with the much complicated model R.M.-Reader + Verifier, which includes several components, our model still outperforms by 0.7 in terms of F1 score.\n\nIt shows that it is important to make balance between these two components: the span detector and unanswerable classifier.\n\nConclusion\tTo sum up, we proposed a simple yet efficient model based on SAN.",
